ADDENDA <Presidential Decree No. 33360, Mar. 28, 2023>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Decree shall enter into force on March 31, 2023.
Article 2 (Applicability to requirements for graduation)
The requirements for graduation from initial training courses under the amended provisions of Article 17(2) shall begin to apply to persons who enter initial training courses after this Decree enters into force.
Article 3 (General transitional measures)
Any disposition, procedure, or other act taken under the previous Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed to have been taken under the corresponding provisions of this Decree.
Article 4 (Transitional measures concerning Firefighting Education and Training Policy Committee)
(1) The Firefighting Education and Training Policy Committee established under the previous Article 2(1) of the Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed the Firefighting Education and Training Policy Committee under the amended provisions of Article 3(1).
(2) Members of the Firefighting Education and Training Policy Committee under the previous Article 2(3) of the Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed members under the amended provisions of Article 3(3).
Article 5 (Transitional measures concerning education and training, such as initial training)
(1) The previous provisions shall apply to initial training, command competency training, and specialized training being conducted under Article 8 of the previous Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials before this Decree enters into force.
(2) A person who has completed or is undergoing education or training entered in the left column of the following table as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed to have completed or be undergoing the education or training entered in the right column of that table.<tbl_group>Initial trainingInitial training under the amended provisions of subparagraph 1a of Appendix 1Command competency training (for deputy fire chiefs and fire captains)Management competency training under the amended provisions of subparagraph 1b of Appendix 1Command competency training (for fire chiefs)Firefighting policy manager training under the amended provisions of subparagraph 1c of Appendix 1Specialized training (including cases where a person is deemed to have completed specialized training under Article 8 of the Addenda)Specialized education and training under the amended provisions of subparagraph 2 of Appendix 1</tbl_group>Article 6 (Transitional measures concerning persons who fail to meet the passing score for completion)
Notwithstanding the amended provisions of Article 19(1), a person who, under Article 17 of the previous Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials as at the time this Decree enters into force, is required to undergo education and training again because his or her education and training performance falls short of the passing score for completion shall be required to undergo education and training again, limited to 1 occasion.
Article 7 (Transitional measures concerning operation of teaching personnel)
Teaching personnel [persons appointed as instructors under the previous Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials (referring to the Regulations before amendment by Presidential Decree No. 19761) as of De cember 21, 2006, the date on which the partially amended Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials (Presidential Decree No. 19761) entered into force, shall be deemed persons appointed as teaching personnel under the partially amended Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials (Presidential Decree No. 19761), and such teaching personnel shall be included], assistant instructors, and lecturers under Article 18 of the previous Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials as at the time this Decree enters into force shall be deemed teaching personnel under the amended provisions of Article 20(1).
Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning persons who have completed job training)
A person who had completed job training under the previous Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials (referring to the Regulations before amendment by Presidential Decree No. 19761) as of December 21, 2006, the date on which the partially amended Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials (Presidential Decree No. 19761) entered into force, shall be deemed to have completed specialized training under the partially amended Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials (Presidential Decree No. 19761).
Article 9 (Transitional measures concerning change in name of special training)
A person who had completed special training under the previous Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials (referring to the Regulations before amendment by Presidential Decree No. 22546) as of December 27, 2010, the date on which the partially amended Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials (Presidential Decree No. 22546) entered into force, shall be deemed to have completed entrusted education and training under this Decree.
Article 10 (Transitional measures concerning scope of application of previous Addenda)
The provisions of the Addenda resulting from amendments to the previous Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials before this Decree enters into force shall continue to remain in force after this Decree enters into force, except for provisions which have already ceased to have effect due to the lapse of a period, etc.
Article 11 Omitted.
Article 12 (Relationship to other statutes or regulations)
If other statutes or regulations in force as at the time this Decree enters into force cite provisions of the previous Regulations on the Education and Training of Firefighting Officials and corresponding provisions exist in this Decree, such citations shall be deemed to cite the corresponding provisions of this Decree in lieu of the previous provisions.

